# Architecture Rules

## Folder structure

```
api/[group]/[...path].js   # Vercel Functions — one catch-all per group
src/                        # React frontend
models/                     # Mongoose schemas (PascalCase.js)
controllers/                # Business logic (camelCase.js)
middleware/auth.js          # requireAuth, requireAdmin only
services/emailService.js
utils/                      # validators, slots, passwordUtils
lib/mongoose.js             # cached connection — ONLY connection point
scripts/                    # one-off scripts
public/                     # static assets
```

## Non-negotiable

- Single `package.json` and `pnpm-lock.yaml` at root
- Single `vercel.json` and `vite.config.js` at root
- No `backend/` or `frontend/` subdirs with own configs
- No Express in `api/` handlers
- Every handler: `await connectDB()` first, `405` last

## Handler skeleton

```js
import { connectDB } from "../../lib/mongoose.js";
import { requireAuth, requireAdmin } from "../../middleware/auth.js";

export default async function handler(req, res) {
  await connectDB();
  const path = req.url.replace(/^\/api\/group/, "").replace(/\?.*/, "");
  const id   = path.match(/^\/([^/]+)$/)?.[1];
  // routes here
  res.status(405).json({ mensaje: "Método no permitido." });
}
```
